const ownership=[['You / Vireal','Accountable for strategy and complete delivery coordination: website, creative, media, outreach, onboarding, measurement coordination, customer/provider support and offline execution.','Assign your internal team; manage developer/specialist dependencies; keep the client informed of scope and blockers.'],['CasaDoctors / authorized CasaTech owners','Business approvals, owned assets/access, actual service facts, financial authority, product/clinical operating decisions and incident escalation.','Confirm named owners, permitted workflows, actual support/service hours and binding provider/payment terms.'],['App / technical delivery','Build, integrate and test role/address/availability/payment/video changes, security and operational reporting.','Vireal coordinates execution; confirm available developer and accepted scope before promising build dates.'],['Qualified professional / privacy / legal reviewers','Assess service suitability, credentials, professional authority, consent/data rules and local requirements.','Review is a dependency, not work a marketing approval can replace.'],['Participating providers / operators','Deliver approved services, maintain capacity and credentials, accept requests, record completion and handle category obligations.','Sign terms; train staff/backup; provide real availability and accountable exception contacts.']];
const sections=[
 section('s1','Care where life happens','My recommendation: build a home-service network people can use for themselves, their family or their pets. Make appropriate video consultations the second priority.',
 p('A son is in the United States. His mother is in Egypt. She needs a suitable consultation, but arranging the visit means coordinating the right professional, her address, a time she can receive them and the payment. The son wants to help from where he is. His mother needs a service that respects her choices and privacy.',
 'I want CasaDoctors to make that coordination clearer. The customer chooses who needs the service and where it should happen. A qualified provider makes suitable services available within the area and hours they can actually cover. Booking and payment happen through a tested app journey; delivery happens at the supported address, or by an appropriate video consultation.',
 'This is the strategic direction, not a claim that every step is already built. We will first prove a small home-doctor service, then add video and other categories when their operating requirements are ready.')+
 box('Our two-sided proposition','Customers arrange care where they need it. Providers choose when they are available to deliver it.')+
 table(['The first three bets','Why I recommend it','What must be proven'],[['Home services first','Directly addresses travel and family-coordination needs.','Qualified capacity, suitable cases, travel, household access and completed visits.'],['Video second','Adds a useful option where a professional can safely deliver remotely.','Scope, recipient location, consent, secure joining and failed-call recovery.'],['A local network before broad expansion','A small dependable area is more useful than a broad menu with no available service.','Real coverage by address and time window, support and sustainable delivery.']])+
 p('Our first 90 days will prepare the channels, recruit and activate providers, repair product gaps and run a bounded home-service pilot. The year then deepens what works, adds separately approved categories and considers an adjacent area. I am not recommending an all-category national launch.')),
 section('s23','Vezeeta Campaigns','Historical creative references, followed by what I would apply to the new home-first model.',p('The useful lesson is to begin with an experience people recognize. For CasaDoctors, that is arranging a visit for someone you care about, sometimes from another country. I would show the recipient, the address and the real confirmation step before asking for an action.','Kairo identifies app downloads as the objective of “90 Million Doctors.” I will use installations as a diagnostic, then judge our service through actual completed episodes, quality and acquisition costs. The other portfolio assets help us study framing; they do not prove which media mix caused Vezeeta’s growth.','The campaign videos below remain references, not a complete advertising archive or an endorsement. Our creative will show home visits and appropriate remote care, not a clinic waiting-room journey. No automatic free-commission offer is carried into this revision.')),
 section('s5','The opportunity and the alternatives','Egypt has reachable digital audiences and existing home-care alternatives. Our case must be more specific than “another booking app”.',
 p('DataReportal’s Digital 2026 Egypt report records 98.2m internet users, 82.7% penetration and 51.6m social-media identities in late 2025. Its advertising estimates include Facebook 51.6m, YouTube 49.3m, TikTok 48.8m adults and Instagram 21.7m. Audiences overlap and definitions differ; these are not A+ households or demand estimates. <a href="https://datareportal.com/reports/digital-2026-egypt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the DataReportal / We Are Social / Meltwater report ↗</a>.',
 'My implication is to test a clear story through Meta and useful service-intent pages through Google. We will choose audiences from actual geography and need-based research, without targeting private medical histories or assuming Instagram proves affluence.',
 'WHO estimates out-of-pocket payments at 54.9% of Egypt’s health expenditure in 2022. This historical financing context supports making fees and payment responsibility easy to understand; it does not estimate our market size. <a href="https://applications.emro.who.int/docs/9789292746926-eng.pdf#page=17" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WHO strategy, printed page 7 ↗</a>.')+
 table(['Alternative','What the public proposition tells us','What I would do differently / prove'],[['Vezeeta','Egypt home visits and a home-visit inquiry route already exist.','Lead with caregiver coordination and address-based delivery; prove the service before claiming an advantage.'],['CliniDo','Its Egypt FAQ describes home visits, remote consultations and lab tests.','Home-first and multiple categories are not exclusive. Make the specific recipient, time and follow-through experience clear.'],['Direct labs: Al Borg / El Mokhtabar type','Home diagnostic collection is already a familiar category. Al Borg’s publisher listing describes scheduling home visits; Almokhtabar’s indexed page advertises house visits.','They are examples and potential alternatives, not confirmed partners. A partnership must add useful coordination without breaking their sample/result process.'],['Individual providers / pharmacies / local veterinary clinics','Direct calls, referrals and existing relationships are practical alternatives; local usage remains to be researched.','Ask what people value today. Earn switching through dependable availability, clarity and support, not by dismissing personal trust.']])+
 box('What we can claim now','Our chosen proposition is home-first care coordination with provider-controlled availability. We cannot claim exclusivity, superior app UX, faster arrival, larger supply or lower prices without a like-for-like test.')+
 p('Home and family care can be a high-value problem with uneven frequency. That limits how often a household should need to book and makes indiscriminate repeat-purchase targets inappropriate. Build useful saved details, trusted providers, education and referrals that make the platform remembered when needed. The frequency and willingness to switch remain research questions.')),
 section('s25','Service priorities and launch geography','One platform can have several categories. Each category still needs a complete operating service.',
 p('My first offer is scheduled, non-emergency adult home-doctor consultations in a researched Fifth Settlement / New Cairo cluster anchored around North Lotus. Use an approximately 5 km starting catchment for research, then define actual coverage by travel time, provider starting location, access and service windows. A radius on a map is not a delivery promise.',
 'Recommend an initial proposed booking-support window of Sunday–Thursday, 10:00–18:00 Cairo, with visits finishing inside an actually covered operating period. Provider evening availability is worth researching, but we will not advertise it until corresponding acceptance, support, travel and escalation coverage is arranged. The calendar examples are not approved working hours.',
 'Video is second priority: prepare it during the home pilot and release a small approved cohort no earlier than D75 if its own checks pass; otherwise hold it into M4. For the first remote-care release, keep the recipient physically in the approved Egypt jurisdiction. A relative can book from abroad, but that does not authorize the clinician to practice across borders.',
 'A veterinary home pilot can follow in M4 if separately ready. Nursing is task-based and needs its own professional scope. In M5–6, consider diagnostics or pharmacy delivery one at a time after operator agreements and recovery tests. Care-product commerce is a later decision, not a condition for launch.')+
 table(['Release','Recommended first scope','Reason / release boundary'],[['First · D61 home pilot','Eligible adult home-doctor visits in one accepted area.','Prove one meaningful service end to end; 8-provider target is proposed capacity input, not a substitute for useful windows.'],['Second · earliest D75 / M4','One professionally approved video scope.','Keep home quality stable; independently test consent, location, joining, records and failures.'],['Next · M4+','Veterinary home visits and/or narrowly scoped nursing, each independently gated.','Different professionals, cases, equipment, safety, documentation and support paths.'],['Then · M5–6+','One signed diagnostics OR pharmacy partner pilot at a time.','Sample/result custody differs from stock/prescription/delivery custody.'],['Evaluate · M7+','Relevant care products and adjacent-area expansion.','Only after core evidence, accountable sellers and sustainable service capacity.']])+
 box('Booking country ≠ service country','For the US–Egypt story, the booker may be in the US, while the professional and recipient are in the approved Egypt service area. Access, OTP, international cards, currencies and terms still need verification. No worldwide provider network or global clinical license is implied.')+
 p('Expand first into an adjacent workable area with its own providers, travel rules and support, not a national announcement. Consider another country only after a separate operating entity/partner, professional, privacy, payments and support assessment. International access is a product ambition; international fulfillment is a separate business launch.')),
 section('s26','Customers, caregivers and the address','We will design around the situation, not a narrow age or income label.',
 table(['Audience / situation','What happens','Job to solve','Experience required','Boundary'],D.personas)+
 p('The earlier A+ emphasis becomes a service-quality standard, rather than a claim that only affluent customers need home care. Older adults, people with limited mobility, local caregivers and relatives abroad have different priorities and purchasing power. We will test practical willingness to pay, trust and assisted-booking needs in the first area.',
 'The initial proposed research sample is 12 adults/caregivers, including at least four arranging care for someone else and, where reachable, four living outside the recipient’s city/country; groups may overlap. Include recipient voices where appropriate and eight relevant providers. These are exploratory samples, not representative market statistics. Ask for their last real experience before showing our concept.',
 'Test: who made the decision, who consented, who paid, which address mattered, what home service was appropriate, how long coordination took, what alternatives they trusted and what made the fee acceptable. Ask providers about actual evening capacity, travel, unsuitable cases and cancellations. Log objections and use them to revise the offer at D14.')),
 section('s27','How the service journeys should work','Seven proposed journeys, each with the booker, recipient, address and accountable professional or seller made explicit.',
 box('Design requirement, not a completed feature list','The interactive journey selector shows the intended experience and the checks needed before release. No live booking, payment or clinical consultation is performed here.')+
 p('A customer must be able to tell the difference between a request, acceptance, payment and confirmation. I recommend reserving capacity, authorizing payment and capturing after provider acceptance where the payment partner supports it. If the existing system instead collects before acceptance, it must explicitly show pending status and provide tested rejection/refund handling. Finance and technical owners choose one supported flow before pilot.',
 'A provider who rejects or does not respond within the agreed request window does not create a confirmed appointment. Release the slot hold and recover payment under the approved policy. Offer alternatives with customer agreement. Do not silently substitute the professional, service mode, pet/human service or service address.',
 'On completion, the professional records the service, finance reconciles the eligible transaction and the authorized customer receives a receipt and next-step information. Clinical records and diagnostic results go through the approved private route, with permissions independent of payment.')),
 section('s10','Providers: useful time, realistic commitments','Make your available time useful. Choose when you work and receive relevant requests within the area and services you support.',
 p('The promise to a provider is control and relevance, not guaranteed bookings or earnings. An evening opening only helps if the professional can travel, deliver the approved service and get support during that window. CasaBusiness should make those constraints explicit.',
 'Recruit individual qualified doctors, eligible home-care professionals and veterinarians as professional tracks. Recruit pharmacies, labs, diagnostic businesses and suitable merchants as operating-business tracks. Ownership, permitted service scope, staff verification, fulfillment responsibility and commercial terms differ. A single generic signup form is not enough.')+
 table(['Stage','Vireal delivery','Activation evidence'],[['Identify and qualify','Research providers actually able and willing to visit the launch area; discuss the service, travel, case suitability and available hours.','Relevant professional/business decision maker; category fit; no assumption that an advertised clinic profile means home-visit capacity.'],['Demonstrate','Show service/area/calendar setup, request acceptance, payment status, completion and statements.','Provider/reception can explain the workflow and operational limits.'],['Verify and contract','Coordinate identity, professional/business eligibility, equipment, qualified scope review and signed schedules.','Valid documents, renewal dates, category/service/mode, charges, commission, payout account and contacts.'],['Configure','Set exact service, price inclusions, area, duration, travel buffer, windows and response expectation.','Valid slots and conflict protection; clear paused/unavailable state.'],['Train and test','Provider and backup handle a safe test, change request, cancellation, support case and statement example.','Observed test completion and signed activation checklist.'],['Maintain','Recheck slots, response behavior, credential changes, travel delays, continuation and statements.','A profile counts as bookable only while capacity and process remain valid.']])+
 p('Proposed initial cadence: 10 suitable researched accounts per week, 8 qualified conversations, 4 demos and 2 activation sessions when team and provider availability support it. These activity targets will be calibrated after D14; 20 qualified conversations and six demos by D30 are the initial phase target, not an additive guarantee. Eight usable home-doctor providers by D60 is the pilot supply proposal. Narrow the area/windows when actual supply is smaller; do not promote inactive profiles to meet a number.',
 'Availability should be published at least a week ahead as an initial operating proposal and reconfirmed daily on active service days. Define a capacity-tested request response window at onboarding; the pilot design target is 15 staffed minutes. That provider acceptance target is separate from the support desk’s critical acknowledgement target. Expired requests recover visibly; home travel and video calls cannot overlap.')),
 section('s28','A community built on useful local service','For launch, community means knowing which participating professionals can actually serve your area.',
 table(['Essential for launch','Why it helps','What waits'],[['Accurate professional profiles and permitted credentials','People can understand service, area, mode and availability.','Popularity rankings or unsupported “best doctor” claims.'],['Address-based discovery and current capacity','The network is relevant to the recipient’s location.','Public live-location maps or precise home addresses visible to other users.'],['Permissioned service communication','Booking changes reach the right person without exposing health details.','Open group medical advice or unmoderated customer/provider chatrooms.'],['Private feedback and report route','Find service problems and act on them.','Public reviews until completion verification, consent, moderation and appeals work.'],['Reviewed practical education','Explain home visits, video suitability and preparing for the service.','Personalized diagnoses, public patient stories or promotional treatment recommendations.']])+
 p('Later, we can test local provider introductions, professionally reviewed educational sessions, consented service reviews and community liaison partnerships. A resident group can share a public link; it should not hand us a member list or invite people to post symptoms publicly.',
 'If we build social features, define moderation capacity, reporting, professional boundaries, misleading-claim review and record-retention rules first. Customer privacy and clinical responsibility stay with the approved systems. A helpful local network does not require a social feed on Day 1.')),
 section('s29','The product and operating requirements','The marketing promise becomes a release checklist, not a collection of attractive screens.',
 table(['Priority','Requirement','Acceptance scope','Owner','Target window'],requirements)+
 p('P0 means required for the affected initial lane; international-booker P0 can hold that lane while a separately accepted local self-booking pilot proceeds. P1 means separately gated next service; P2 is later evaluation. Any gap affecting safety, identity, payment or consent blocks its scope regardless of priority label.',
 'The app comparison is still an evidence task. Capture CasaDoctors and relevant alternatives using the same scenarios: selecting someone else’s address, choosing a suitable home visit, understanding the total fee, acceptance and confirmation, cancellation/refund and provider availability. Record build/date, device, successful steps and failure recovery. Stop before real bookings or money unless an approved safe test arrangement exists. Do not use this plan’s illustrations as real app screenshots.',
 'The website rebuild should lead with “Home services” and a separate “Video consultations” path, then caregiver, veterinary, diagnostics/pharmacy readiness and provider partnership pages. Add how-it-works, actual coverage/hours, price/terms, qualified provider information, accessible help and privacy. Unsupported categories show preparation status or remain unpublished. A “book” button must reach a real supported flow.',
 '<a href="https://mmetwally23.github.io/casadoctors-plan-site/prototype.html?revision=homefirst21#home" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Home-first website prototype ↗</a> now demonstrates the family, recipient-address, permission, acceptance and payment-status journey in English and Egyptian Arabic. It uses fictional details; it is not evidence that the app requirements are built or services are live.')),
 section('s12','Customer support and provider success','Vireal will run both service queues and coordinate escalation with CasaDoctors and the qualified operators.',
 p('Set up a customer/caregiver queue and a provider/business queue before D17 inquiries begin. Use a helpdesk/CRM with case ownership, reason codes, timestamps, consented contacts and escalation logs; choose the tool after access and data review. Provider onboarding and account questions should not bury a disrupted home visit.',
 'The initial coverage proposal is Sunday–Thursday, 10:00–18:00 Cairo, subject to an actual named roster and backup. Schedule service and request handling inside genuinely supported windows. An evening provider slot cannot go live until operating support and escalation cover it. If hours expand, update provider availability, customer pages and workload capacity together. We make no 24/7 commitment.',
 'Pilot targets are at least 90% of nonurgent first human responses within four staffed hours and 95% of booking-critical acknowledgements within 15 staffed minutes. Growth raises nonurgent compliance to 95%; critical acknowledgement remains 95%. Acknowledgement is not resolution. Clinical/safety events are escalated immediately through the approved professional/on-call route, not held in a customer-service timer.')+
 table(['Case','First handling','Accountable escalation / closure'],[['Recipient cannot be reached / access denied','Verify authorized contact and service location privately; contact the provider and apply the waiting/no-show rule.','Operations resolves reschedule/cancel/fee treatment with evidence.'],['Provider delay / unaccepted request','Show actual pending/delay status; offer permitted alternatives with consent.','Provider success/operations; no silent substitution.'],['Payer abroad asks for clinical details','Check permission; provide only authorized booking/payment information.','Qualified privacy/clinical owner handles records or representation question.'],['Payment pending / refund / dispute','Check the payment ledger, not a screenshot alone; avoid duplicate charge.','Finance/payment partner records outcome, original-method refund and expected timing.'],['Video connection or suitability issue','Help rejoin within agreed window or trigger reviewed recovery.','Clinician determines clinical next step; support coordinates reschedule/refund.'],['Home-visit safety / serious incident','Follow immediate safety and professional escalation procedure; protect involved people.','Named CasaTech/qualified incident owner, backup, private evidence and follow-up.'],['Pharmacy / lab / pet-care exception','Route to the actual accountable operator; do not answer specialist questions as general support.','Pharmacist/lab clinical lead/veterinarian handles professional decision; support coordinates.']])+
 p('Before the home pilot, rehearse at least six representative cases, including an unreachable recipient, a provider delay, a payer/recipient permission conflict, a refund, a safety escalation and a video recovery. Time the handoffs, confirm actual backup availability and use observed handling time to cap new requests. Review backlog and service cases every active day.',
 'The supplied agreement calls for suspected personal-data breach notification without undue delay and within 24 hours of discovery, and serious incidents immediately with a 24-hour outer limit. These are reporting terms from the template, not permission to wait or a complete statement of legal duties. Publish named escalation contacts and have qualified owners confirm applicable requirements.')),
 section('s13','Customer and provider acquisition','Introduce the home-first idea, recruit usable supply, then acquire only the service volume we can support.',
 table(['Route','Concrete work','Objective / measure','When'],[['Meta · customers','Caregiver story, self-booking home service, recipient-address explainer and separately gated video/pet concepts.','Before pilot: comprehension and relevant interest. After gate: first completed services and quality.','D17 awareness; bounded booking from D62 after acceptance.'],['Google · customers','Separate service/area intent pages and search groups; location settings matched to the address/coverage model.','Useful eligible visits, valid requests and mature first-completion acquisition.','Small prelaunch informational test; actual service intent only when live.'],['Meta / Google · providers','Service-specific availability pitch and qualified demo inquiry; direct professional outreach does the heavier early work.','Discussion→demo→signed→verified→bookable, plus usable slots.','P2 recruitment; maintained where supply gaps exist.'],['Content / organic search','How to arrange a home visit for a parent; how address/consent/payment work; video limitations; provider workflow.','Useful discovery, clear questions, accurate local pages and completion paths.','Foundations M1; deepen from real questions monthly.'],['Partners','Caregiver/residential/employer liaisons, relevant professional businesses and diaspora community links where permitted.','Opt-in introductions and attributed first completions; no personal-data handover.','Research P2; one bounded test after service proof.'],['Referrals','Neutral public service link after a genuine completion; optional reward only after terms/professional review.','Referred first completions and quality; no reward for medical frequency or positive reviews.','M3 design; M6–8 controlled test.'],['Offline','Approved building/clinic/pharmacy partner materials, local banners and street-screen placements where permitted.','Verified delivery plus attributable inquiries/completions; separate modeled exposure.','P2 site research; P3 production; P4 small execution only if approved.']])+
 p('For a booker in another country, the landing page asks where the recipient needs service. Do not market provider coverage across the US just because we show the son there. I propose a small US-based Egyptian-community hypothesis first, only after customer terms, payment access and the actual US-booker/Egypt-recipient tests pass. Other countries need their own access/payment review.',
 'Avoid targeting individual health conditions, inferred diagnoses or patient/customer lists containing sensitive information. Clinical intake, prescription uploads, test names/results and recipient details belong in reviewed private systems. Check current platform policies and permitted measurement at campaign preflight; nothing here launches an ad account or campaign.',
 'Stop the affected campaign when the destination breaks, claims become inaccurate, supply disappears or a critical service/payment/privacy issue emerges. Weekly reviews should explain changes in useful requests, completions, cancellations and support load. Clicks, installs and followers do not prove a working care service.')),
 section('s30','Media buying: what runs, for whom and why','The digital split is a starting test proposal, expressed as percentages of a separately approved amount. No annual budget or financial forecast is included.',
 table(['Stage','Meta customers','Google customers','Meta providers','Google providers'],[['Awareness / supply · D17–60','45%','10%','35%','10%'],['Home pilot · D61–90','35%','40%','20%','5%'],['Proven growth · M4+','30%','45%','20%','5%']])+
 p('These percentages sum to 100% at each stage. They exclude production, tools, field work, offline placement and staffing, which are scoped separately. The local customer and diaspora tests are subdivisions of the customer allocation; they are not extra percentages added to it. As a starting restriction, keep the unproven diaspora lane at no more than 20% of customer media and only after its gate. If the gate is held, keep that amount unspent or reassign it through an explicit test review.',
 'Build four distinct reporting cells: customer Meta, customer Google, provider Meta and provider Google. Within customers, separate local/abroad-booker, home/video/vet and original/new area. Use clear naming and source tags. Do not fragment the first small test into every possible audience and category simultaneously.')+
 table(['Cell','Starting setup','Creative / destination','Decision'],[['Customer Meta','Awareness/reach or explanatory video before service release; eligible conversion goal only after reliable measurement.','Mother-at-home story and three-identities explainer; accurate prelaunch or supported service page.','Two concepts, then one-variable changes; report exposure and comprehension separately from conversions.'],['Customer Google','Separate home-doctor area intent and caregiver explainer; test actual queries and exclusions.','Example research terms: doctor home visit New Cairo / دكتور زيارة منزلية التجمع; no search volume assumed.','Exclude irrelevant clinic-only, jobs, unsupported locations/services and emergency intent; privacy/policy review first.'],['Provider Meta','Professional offer and workflow demonstration; qualification questions without customer medical data.','Available time + travel-aware timetable; provider inquiry with category/area/hours.','Follow up on staffed commercial days; judge qualified discussion and activation, not cheap form fills.'],['Provider Google','Small provider-partnership intent experiment only where actual useful demand exists.','Category-specific partnership page.','If meaningful intent is absent, pause the cell and propose reassignment to direct outreach or a better paid test.']])+
 p('First 14 active awareness days: inspect delivery and inquiry handling daily; diagnose creative/message after a full usable observation window rather than reacting to a single day. Review frequency around 2–4 as a planning diagnostic, not an optimum or promise. Initial reach targets are set from the approved amount and eligible audience at D14; no funded reach is implied today.',
 'Pilot pacing is capped by bookable capacity and actual handling load. At each weekly review, reconcile spend and a disclosed 30-day first-completion cohort, show conversion lag and unattributed customers, and compare media-only and all-in acquisition cost. Finance sets a category-specific acceptable acquisition ceiling from observed contribution. If a cell reaches three times that agreed ceiling with no mature first completion, investigate and hold/revise it; this is a diagnostic rule, not statistical proof.',
 'A test brief states audience, mechanism, readiness, one changed variable, primary outcome, observation window and stop condition. For small pilots, use qualitative and operational evidence honestly; do not claim significance from a handful of bookings. Scaling requires four active weeks of stable quality and no unresolved critical issue.')),
 section('s19','Offline, partnerships and useful referrals','Vireal will plan and execute approved offline activity in the area the service can actually cover.',
 p('I would begin with a small permissioned local footprint: one residential/community route, relevant reception/pharmacy materials and a carefully chosen banner or street-screen test. Ask vendors for site, dimensions, visibility, dates, actual play commitments, permissions and a written delivery scope. A large screen is not automatically a better investment than a trusted local introduction.')+
 table(['Phase','Vireal delivery','Completion / outcome'],[['P2 · D28','Research local banner and street-screen inventory; identify permission owners, suppliers and community liaisons.','Shortlist with catchment, vendor scope/quote, permissions and measurement limits; no booking claimed.'],['P3 · D55–56','Produce actual-size home-first banner/screen adaptations after approval; test QR, short URL and support route.','Creative proof approved, service status accurate, signed placement scope and delivery plan.'],['P4 · D66 onward if accepted','Execute bounded placements and inspect reception materials / screen delivery weekly.','Photos, placement dates and vendor play logs; source-tagged visits/inquiries and deduplicated first completions where attributable.'],['P5–6','Review after four active weeks; renew useful placements, change creative/site or stop.','Keep verified delivery separate from modeled reach; compare source outcomes and service quality before renewal.']])+
 p('Banner concept: “رعاية للي يهمّك، لحد البيت.” Pair a calm doorway scene with “شوف الخدمات المتاحة على عنوانك” and a unique QR. Street screen: show a son choosing his mother’s Egypt address, then the accepted provider/time—not a flashing list of every future category. On a small reception card, show the actual service area, published hours, next step and a readable support route.',
 'Use a neutral partnership introduction: a community liaison shares our public explanation and people choose to contact us. No resident, employee, patient or diaspora-member list is handed over. A co-branded material needs written partner/brand permission and accurate status. El Mokhtabar and Al Borg are not available logos or partners by default.',
 'Start referrals with a shareable service page, not a relative’s booking details. Any later reward needs approved terms, fraud controls, professional review and a cap; it cannot require a positive review, encourage unnecessary care or imply clinical endorsement. Report referral completions and service quality, not just links shared.')),
 section('s31','Slogans, voice and campaign examples','Natural English and Egyptian Arabic. These are new proposals for this direction, not tested campaign winners.',
 table(['Purpose','English','Egyptian Arabic'],[['Recommended brand line','Care that comes to you.','الرعاية تيجي لحد عندك.'],['Family / caregiver option','Care for them. From wherever you are.','رتّب لهم الرعاية، من مكانك.'],['Home-service option','The right care. At their address.','رعاية مناسبة، على عنوانهم.'],['Provider line','Make your available time useful.','وقتك المتاح، خلّيه لخدمة تناسبك.']])+
 p('My recommended customer story keeps the son and mother human: the distance is familiar, but her address, consent and chosen time make it practical. Premium here means calm clarity and follow-through. Avoid miracle reassurance, “best doctor”, universal instant availability or “كل حاجة في أي وقت”.')+
 '<div class="copy-pair"><div lang="en"><small>CUSTOMER · LIVE ONLY AFTER RELEVANT TESTS</small><h3>You are far away.<br>Her care can still be close.</h3><p>Arrange a suitable home visit for your mother at her address in Egypt. See available providers, the fee and how confirmation works. Pay through the supported app methods, with booking updates shared according to her permissions.</p><b>Check services at her address.</b></div><div dir="rtl" lang="ar"><small>العميل · بعد جاهزية الخدمة</small><h3>إنت بعيد.<br>بس تقدر ترتّب لها الرعاية وهي في بيتها.</h3><p>اختار عنوان مامتك في مصر، وشوف الخدمات والمواعيد المتاحة هناك. تعرف السعر وخطوات التأكيد، وتدفع من خلال وسائل الدفع المتاحة في التطبيق. وتتابع تفاصيل الحجز المسموح بمشاركتها.</p><b>شوف المتاح على عنوانها.</b></div></div>'+
 '<div class="copy-pair"><div lang="en"><small>PROVIDER · INQUIRY</small><h3>Your time. Your area.<br>Services you can deliver.</h3><p>Make suitable home visits available in the areas and hours you choose. Review relevant requests, leave time for travel and follow a clear acceptance and payment process.</p><b>Explore a CasaDoctors partnership.</b></div><div dir="rtl" lang="ar"><small>مقدم الخدمة · تعرّف على الشراكة</small><h3>وقتك ومنطقتك.<br>وخدمات تقدر تلتزم بيها.</h3><p>حدّد الزيارات اللي تقدر تقدمها، والمنطقة والمواعيد المناسبة ليك. راجع الطلبات، وسيب وقت للمشوار، واعرف خطوات القبول والدفع بوضوح.</p><b>اعرف تفاصيل الشراكة مع كازا دكتورز.</b></div></div>'+
 box('Prelaunch wording','“We are preparing home services in selected Egypt areas. Explore the idea or discuss joining the provider network.” / “بنجهّز خدمات منزلية في مناطق محددة في مصر. اعرف الفكرة، أو اتكلم معانا لو حابب تقدم خدماتك.” Never run the live booking copy against an unverified service.')+
 p('Voice rules: short sentences; concrete place/time/payment details; respectful Egyptian Arabic; no generic corporate promises. Speak to the person doing the arranging while respecting the person receiving care. Veterinary creative uses pet-owner language and its own visuals. Video explains suitability. Pharmacy and diagnostics name the real fulfilling operator only after agreement and approval.')),
 section('s2','Six phases, with a clear way forward','Dates are relative planning days from the accepted kickoff. Evidence, capacity and approval—not the date alone—allow the next step.',
 p('The interactive roadmap below is the source of the six phase objectives, deliverables, priority tasks, KPI proposals and exit conditions. Work can overlap where different owners have capacity. At kickoff, map calendar-day positions to real staffed days, weekends and dependencies. A late prerequisite moves the dependent release.',
 'The new home-first model replaces the earlier clinic-pilot targets. I propose eight activated home-doctor providers by D60 and 40 completed home visits in the first 30-day pilot, subject to real capacity and agreement. These are planning targets, not a forecast or proof of demand. Any changes are recorded with a reason and effective date; monthly targets and phase gates use the same register.')),
 section('s3','Day 1–90 priority tasks','Every day has a priority action, owner, dependency and a way to tell whether it is complete.',
 p('A checkmark reports a task, not permission to launch. From D17, active-campaign and inquiry checks repeat every staffed day. From the pilot, check provider availability, travel, service exceptions, support and transaction reconciliation each active day. Weekly reviews compare actuals with the accepted scope.',
 'The dates sequence the work; they do not assume one person can perform every task. You lead Vireal and coordinate the technical, clinical, finance and provider dependencies. App work is a real delivery requirement; a campaign launch cannot substitute for it.')),
 section('s4','Monthly objectives and KPI definitions','One target register powers the roadmap, monthly scorecard and annual appendix.',
 table(['Measure','Definition','Interpretation / window'],D.metrics)+
 p('Every rate is shown with numerator, denominator, period and missing/pending counts. Targets remain proposals until the responsible owners accept them against real supply, media and operating capacity. Report home, video, veterinary, pharmacy, diagnostics and commerce separately, and distinguish local/abroad bookers and service areas. Low counts require case review, not confident conclusions from a percentage.',
 'Proposed quality thresholds are consistent across this plan: pilot fulfillment and arrival compliance ≥90%, provider cancellation ≤10%, nonurgent support ≥90%, critical acknowledgement ≥95%. From growth, fulfillment/arrival and both support compliance targets are ≥95%, provider cancellation ≤5%. Time windows remain four staffed hours for nonurgent first human response and 15 staffed minutes for booking-critical acknowledgement. A critical safety/payment/privacy failure blocks its lane regardless of average KPI success.')),
 section('s8','Measurement and the operating stack','Measure the marketing journey without sending private care information into ad tools.',
 table(['Layer','What Vireal coordinates','Acceptance'],[['Owned assets','Client-owned Meta/Google assets, domain, app-store access and permission register.','Named admins, recovery, billing authority and no duplicate setup.'],['Website','GTM + GA4 for neutral page/CTA/inquiry events and source tags, with reviewed consent behavior.','D13 QA: no duplicate events or sensitive URL/form payloads.'],['App','Developer-integrated Firebase / app analytics with neutral journey states where permitted.','D36–37 test-build QA; private operational reconciliation before booking acquisition.'],['CRM / helpdesk','Provider qualification stages, customer/provider queues, owners and timestamps.','Correct routing, restricted data and measured support response.'],['Private service ledger','Request, accepted, paid, confirmed, completed, canceled, refunded and payable records.','Finance/service source of truth; controlled access and audit trail.'],['Reporting','Weekly audience/service/area results and monthly mature cohorts.','Disclosed source, attribution lag, actual counts, pending and cost definitions.']])+
 p('Avoid sending names, phone numbers, addresses, diagnoses, prescriptions, symptoms, test results, detailed health URLs or payment credentials into analytics or advertising. Even a service name can reveal health information; qualified privacy/technical owners approve the event map. Do not assume every completion can be uploaded as a platform conversion. Use permitted aggregate reporting and private reconciliation.',
 'Acquisition needs accurate destinations and source tags. Activation needs verified supply and completed service states. Retention needs consented appropriate follow-up and closed cohorts. Referral needs a neutral source mechanism. Revenue needs signed terms and private finance truth. No connector availability or planning diagram means these integrations are already deployed.')),
 section('s15','Retention, referrals and commercial logic','A useful care service is remembered when needed; we should not manufacture medical demand to raise repeat rates.',
 p('Activation is the first completed eligible service, on both sides: the customer understands and receives it; the provider can deliver and reconcile it. Registration and app installation are intermediate steps. After completion, make receipts, authorized saved addresses, help and consented feedback easy to find.',
 'Use transactional messages for actual booking changes and professional next steps. Marketing consent is separate. A caregiver may receive allowed status updates but not automatic medical histories/results. Later lifecycle tests can remind people of saved details or explain service availability; clinically necessary follow-up remains a professional decision, not a marketing trigger.',
 'Track whether households return for appropriate needs and whether providers remain active with usable slots. Review mature 90-day cohorts by category rather than applying subscription churn or weekly-care targets to everyone. Collect cancellation reasons, support burden and provider effort to understand where value is being lost.')+
 table(['Commercial question','Proposed treatment'],[['How CasaDoctors earns','Individually signed commission/fees on eligible completed transactions under the provider agreement; product/category models need explicit terms.'],['What price the customer sees','Service charge, travel/visit fee, materials/delivery and applicable charges before commitment. Make mode and cancellation differences clear.'],['Why a provider joins','Relevant local demand and manageable control over time/area—not guaranteed bookings or a universal free period.'],['What decides paid growth','Actual earned commission and attributable costs, support/fulfillment burden and acquisition recovery by category.'],['What we will not invent','Universal 15–25% agreement, fixed earnings, LTV, annual budget, financial forecast or a ready global payment network.']])+
 p('Use a separately signed, bounded incentive only if it solves a documented provider objection and economics support it. State the scope, expiry, eligibility and post-promotion terms before communication. The earlier suggestion of free commission is not part of the supplied agreement.')),
 section('s6','Provider agreement and payment responsibilities','The supplied agreement remains the commercial reference. New home/video/category scope must be explicitly accepted, not assumed to be covered.',
 '<div class="agreement-reference">'+VOICE.markdown(A.commercial).split(/\n\s*\n/).map(x=>x.startsWith('|')?table(x.split('\n')[0].split('|').slice(1,-1),x.split('\n').slice(2).filter(Boolean).map(r=>r.split('|').slice(1,-1))):x.startsWith('### ')?'<h3>'+x.slice(4)+'</h3>':p(x)).join('')+'</div>'+
 p('Before each category release, qualified owners review whether this template and its schedules need amendments for home delivery, travel/materials, video, veterinary scope, pharmacy seller/fulfiller, diagnostic collection/results or merchant returns. A general provider template does not itself establish every category’s permission, insurance, professional authority or payment-partner acceptance.',
 'Do not collect payment credentials in this plan. Use approved in-app/payment-partner flows. Receipt, refund, chargeback and service dispute rules must identify the accountable party and original payment method. International issuance/acceptance, exchange rates and fees are disclosed from the actual payment arrangement, not promised from the platform concept.',
 'The earlier agreement review noted annual renewal with 30 days’ written notice, a 15-day cure where applicable and Arabic prevailing for interpretation before Egyptian authorities/courts. These are template summaries requiring appropriate review. No provider is treated as signed merely because the document exists.')),
 section('s14','Who handles what, and what we agree first','Vireal owns delivery coordination. The client-facing plan shows responsibilities and dependencies; staffing-hour estimates stay internal.',
 table(['Who','Responsibility','What needs to be in place'],ownership)+
 table(['When','Point to agree','Why it matters'],[['D1–6','Home-first direction; accountable operating/clinical/technical/finance owners.','A marketing plan cannot approve clinical scope or build app features by itself.'],['D14','First service area, adult home-doctor scope, prelaunch claims and test targets.','Makes the first offer specific enough to research and deliver.'],['Before D17','Actual inquiry coverage, account permissions and separate media test amount.','No unattended inquiries or assumed spending.'],['D31–60','Provider terms, travel/fee rules, recipient consent and supported payment flow.','Defines what the customer and provider actually commit to.'],['D59–60','Home-pilot entry and separate international-booker lane acceptance.','Local self-booking can proceed only under its own evidence if abroad booking is still held.'],['Before video release','Professional scope, recipient location, permissions and call recovery.','Video is a distinct clinical/technical service.'],['D90 and each new category','Growth quality, operator capacity, contribution and category-specific release.','Keeps expansion tied to delivery rather than the annual calendar.']])+
 p('Nothing is marked approved by generating this plan. Use the phase record to capture named approver, date, evidence, decision and permitted scope. Changes to service geography, professional scope or payment flow require review of dependent copy, ads, support and product behavior.')),
 section('s17','What we know, and what still needs proof','This is the capability register for the revised direction, not a certification of the app or business.',
 table(['Status','Current understanding','Evidence / next action'],capabilityRows)+
 '<details><summary>Evidence-readiness audit · scored from supplied materials</summary>'+table(['Area','Evidence score / 5','Basis'],audit)+p('Evidence-readiness total: '+audit.reduce((n,r)=>n+r[1],0)+' / 85. This scores what has been evidenced in the supplied material, not the quality of unseen software or the team’s ability. No new live app/admin audit has been completed. The pattern is clear: the concept has direction, while usable supply, field research, instrumentation and category fulfillment remain the main launch work.')+'</details>'+
 p('The full diagnostic prototype/app comparison, named support roster, signed provider capacity, professional approvals and international payment test results are still material gaps. They have owners and dates in the plan. We can present a clear recommendation today without presenting those future results as completed.')),
 section('s18','Risks and the corrective move','A practical plan says what we do when the assumption is wrong.',
 table(['Trigger','Action','Accountable owner'],[['Too little qualified home supply','Narrow area/windows and strengthen provider activation; hold unsupported ads.','Vireal partnerships + operations'],['Recipient cannot consent / identity unclear','Use reviewed representation route or do not proceed; payer relationship alone is insufficient.','Qualified privacy/clinical owners'],['Unreliable travel / provider safety','Change buffers/area/windows; stop unsafe visit scope and resolve access conditions.','Operations + provider'],['International payment/OTP fails','Hold abroad-booker lane; explain supported alternatives only after approval.','Technical / finance'],['Wrong mode for the case','Qualified professional determines next step; do not sell video as a universal replacement.','Clinical / veterinary lead'],['Refund or slot state inconsistent','Stop affected booking acquisition; reconcile, fix and retest.','Finance + developer'],['Support cannot meet coverage','Reduce acquisition or add genuinely available coverage; restrict service windows.','Vireal support + operations'],['Named partner not contracted','No logo, live service claim or inventory assumption; keep discovery separate.','Partnerships + authorized owners'],['New category weakens core service','Defer it; maintain the proven area and service.','You + CasaDoctors'],['Sensitive information leaks into marketing','Stop affected data flow; follow immediate incident procedure and qualified review.','Technical / privacy / incident owners']])+
 p('Our meeting should answer: why home-first, who it helps, what can launch, who will deliver it, what the app must do, when ads can run and how we know whether it works. Where evidence is missing, the answer is the assigned test and its release condition—not a confident invented claim.')),
 section('s24','Annual marketing appendix','A conditional month-by-month action calendar, with separate customer and provider creative. Month 1 starts at the agreed kickoff.',
 p('Q1 defines and tests the home-first promise. Q2 deepens reliable home care, releases suitable video and considers one category at a time. Q3 builds useful household continuity and local partnerships. Q4 either proves an adjacent area or improves the original one, and reviews relevant commerce only when justified. Calendar selection does not approve a service launch.',
 'For M1–3, plan 10 master assets per month as an initial production proposal: six customer assets (four feed/carousel masters, two short video masters) and four provider assets (two feed/carousel masters, two short video masters). Adaptations are not additional master concepts. Confirm production capacity and review dates at kickoff. Later volumes follow actual learning and available production time rather than an invented year-long output commitment.',
 'Weekly Q1 production follows the daily roadmap: Week 1 approve stories and product truth; Week 2 produce and review with technical/professional owners; Week 3 publish only permitted variants and check handling; Week 4 report learning and prepare the next package. In the first month, paid awareness still waits for D14 checks. No forced seasonal campaign or fabricated customer testimonial is included.',
 'Each campaign below has a specific story, English/Egyptian Arabic hook, format direction, destination, audience, measure and a readiness boundary. A future category’s fallback is useful education or a clearly labeled preparation page—not a misleading booking ad. The monthly target register is shared with the phase scorecard.')),
 section('s32','Sources and revision notes','Home-first revision · 21 October 2026. Strategic recommendations are written from Vireal’s perspective.',
 table(['Use','Source','Date / limitation'],D.sources.map(s=>[s[0],'<a href="'+s[2]+'" target="_blank" rel="noopener">'+s[1]+' ↗</a>',s[3]]))+
 p('The core direction comes from the user’s 21 October 2026 brief. The earlier account/payment/admin statements are client reports, not new verification. The provider agreement is the supplied template previously reviewed; the original PDF is not published here. Sources describe public propositions and historical context, not actual service performance in our selected area.',
 'This revision supersedes the clinic-first pilot, old nearest-clinic positioning, automatic free-trial ideas and old numerical supply/completion targets. The annual budget and financial forecast remain excluded. Earlier local working records are kept under their original browser storage key; this home-first plan starts a separate record so old approvals and checkmarks cannot appear to approve the new model.',
 'The plan’s diagrams are explanations of a proposed operating model. They are not screenshots of the live app, confirmed partnerships, executed campaigns or evidence of a completed service.'))
];
module.exports={sections,table,p,box,requirements,capabilityRows,ownership};
